  "answer": "The umpire shows a red card when the umpire faults a side under Law 16.7.1.2 or 16.7.1.3 (Instructions to Technical Officials 7.0 (5), in force 2025-04-26): “When the Umpire faults a side (Law 16.7.1.2 or 16.7.1.3) the Umpire shall call: “Come here” to the offending player and then call: “… [name of player], fault for misconduct”, followed by a specific explanation of the misconduct (BWF Statutes, Section 4.1.5, Section 5). at the same time raising the right hand holding a red card above the Umpire’s head.” Law 16.7.1.2 applies when “faulting the offending side, if previously warned” (Laws of Badminton 5.0 (2), in force 2025-04-26), and Law 16.7.1.3 applies when “faulting the offending side in cases of flagrant offence or breach” (Laws of Badminton 5.0 (2), in force 2025-04-26). A red card also results from “flagrant or other misbehaviour” (Instructions to Technical Officials 7.0 (5), in force 2025-04-26). Next, “The Umpire must call the Referee on court and report immediately” (Instructions to Technical Officials 7.0 (5), in force 2025-04-26), and “On faulting a side (Law 16.7.1.2 or 16.7.1.3), the umpire shall report the offending side immediately to the Referee, who shall have the power to disqualify the offending side from the match” (Laws of Badminton 5.0 (2), in force 2025-04-26).",
